{"comment_text": {"ja56:0.1": "", "ja56:0.2": "", "ja56:0.3": "", "ja56:0.4": "", "ja56:1.1": "A man discovers a large lump of gold, but must break it into four to make it useful. | The verse is almost identical with the previous, only differing in the key term. ", "ja56:1.2": "As with the previous verse, the key term <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pahaṭṭha</i> rests on both the story and a dual meaning. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Pahaṭṭha</i> normally has the sense “cheerful” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>√haṁs</i>), but the commentary connects it rather with gold that has been forged (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>√ghaṁs</i>) until it is luminous and radiant. ", "ja56:1.3": "", "ja56:1.4": "", "ja56:1.5": "", "ja56:1.6": "", "ja56:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja56:0.1": "<article id='ja56'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja56:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja56:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja56:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja56:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja56:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja56:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja56:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja56:1.5": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja56:1.6": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja56:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja56:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja56:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja56:0.3": "Āsīsavagga ", "ja56:0.4": "6. Kañcanakkhandhajātaka ", "ja56:1.1": "“Yo pahaṭṭhena cittena, ", "ja56:1.2": "pahaṭṭhamanaso naro; ", "ja56:1.3": "Bhāveti kusalaṁ dhammaṁ, ", "ja56:1.4": "yogakkhemassa pattiyā; ", "ja56:1.5": "Pāpuṇe anupubbena, ", "ja56:1.6": "sabbasaṁyojanakkhayan”ti. ", "ja56:2.1": "Kañcanakkhandhajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja56:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 56 ", "ja56:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja56:0.3": "Hope ", "ja56:0.4": "The Mass of Gold: a past life story ", "ja56:1.1": "He whose heart is well-forged, ", "ja56:1.2": "a man of cheerful mind, ", "ja56:1.3": "develops skillful qualities ", "ja56:1.4": "for the sake of sanctuary from the yoke. ", "ja56:1.5": "Gradually he would attain ", "ja56:1.6": "the ending of all fetters. ", "ja56:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja56:0.1": "", "ja56:0.2": "", "ja56:0.3": "", "ja56:0.4": "", "ja56:1.1": "csp1ed22.14, csp2ed22.14, ms22J_123, msdiv56, pts-vp-pli1.278", "ja56:1.2": "", "ja56:1.3": "", "ja56:1.4": "", "ja56:1.5": "", "ja56:1.6": "", "ja56:2.1": "ms22J_124"}, "keys_order": ["ja56:0.1", "ja56:0.2", "ja56:0.3", "ja56:0.4", "ja56:1.1", "ja56:1.2", "ja56:1.3", "ja56:1.4", "ja56:1.5", "ja56:1.6", "ja56:2.1"]}